{title: 20 Cigarettes}
{artist: Morgan Wallen}
{key: A}
{capo: 1}
{tempo: 98}
{comment: Play Am/F/C/G shapes with capo 1 = concert key A. Chart adapted from public chord sheets.}

{start_of_intro: pickup}
|Am| |F| |C| |G|
Vocal and guitar only — "We burned..." enters on B section feel, then D on "13 cigarettes".
{end_of_intro}

{start_of_verse}
Twenty [Am]cigarettes and I [F]lit me one
On that [C]redwood deck on De-[G]monbreun
She was [Am]with her friends, left 'em [F]standin' there
There was [C]more than smoke in that [G]summer air
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
We burnt [F]two while she told me bout' her hometown
She was drinkin' [Am]Titos, said I better slow down
I was like, [C]hell no, I ain't drinkin' by my-[G]self, no
Said she loved my [F]accent so I kept talkin'
Reached for the [Am]pack on the table by my wallet
We tore [C]off to light the [G]night we had [F]left
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
With thirteen [Am]cigarettes and I [F]lit me one
With the [C]windows cracked in my [G]old half-ton
Singin' [Am]take me home on them [F]country roads
So I turned [C]off on one then next [G]thing you know
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
We had a beer [F]bottle lookin' like an ashtray
Under that [Am]full moon she was 'bout halfway
Naked in my [C]truck bed, so I helped her with the [Am]rest
She was sayin' [F]my name, barely even knew it
We were both [Am]lyin', said we [G]never do this
To the [G]music of the wind through the [F]woods
{end_of_chorus}

